Technical Specification: Spaceware – Proxima Descent (Version 4)
Active Controls, Inventory & Crafting System

• 1. Control Activation

Controls appear ONLY after the astronaut has exited the ship (post V3 transition). No joystick. No arrow buttons. Four discrete commands: S, J, A, I.

Each executes a mathematical function with clear rules.

• 2. Button S – Scan

Function: Detects buried resources within a short radius.

When activated, temporary icons for Scrap, Food, or Artifacts appear at random locations near the astronaut.

Cooldown: 15 seconds. Cannot scan while cooldown is active.

Implementation:

Code example for AI and human on the loop:
-----------------------------
| if (scanCooldown <= 0) {  |
• revealResources();        •
| scanCooldown = 15;        |
• }                         •
-----------------------------

• 3. Button J – Jump

Function: Allows the astronaut to clear small terrain depressions or reach mid-height resources.

Without jump, movement is limited to flat lateral sliding.

Cooldown: 2 seconds (prevents spam, not a power-up).

Jump is a brief Y-axis displacement. Camera does not change.

• 4. Button A – Attack

**Function:** Fires a plasma projectile (simple SVG) that destroys small obstacles or enemies (when implemented).

Cooldown: 3 seconds. Unlimited ammunition.

Projectile behavior: Instant damage at impact point. Moves horizontally in a straight line from astronaut's position.

• 5. Button I – Inventory

Function: Opens a modal window (no game reload) showing two panels:

• 5.1 Available Materials
- Scrap
- Food
- Artifacts
- Current quantities displayed

• 5.2 Recipes
List of upgrades the player can craft if they have the required materials. Each recipe includes a cost and a clear benefit.

Example Recipes (expandable):

| Upgrade | Cost | Benefit |
|---------|------|---------|
| Enhanced Engine | 20 Scrap + 5 Artifacts | +10% movement speed |
| Hydroponic Farm | 15 Scrap + 10 Food | Generates 1 Food every 30 seconds (passive) |
| Energy Shield | 30 Scrap + 15 Artifacts | Absorbs 1 hit |

• 6. Input Restrictions

- Buttons are NOT customizable. Fixed as S, J, A, I.
- Always visible on UI after V3 phase begins.
- Player can press in any order, respecting cooldowns.
- Ship is no longer visible on surface. Astronaut is the main entity.
- Lateral movement (left/right touch or keyboard) remains active.
- Buttons S, J, A, I are supplements, not replacements for movement.

• 7. Integration with Previous Versions

| Version | Phase | Status |
|---------|-------|--------|
| V1 | Descent (40,000 → 0 altitude) | Preserved |
| V2 | Landing cutscene | Preserved |
| V3 | Surface exploration + resource spawn | Preserved |
| V4 | Active controls + inventory + crafting | Added |

- Resources (Scrap, Food, Artifacts) already exist from passive V3 spawning.
- Scan adds active discovery.
- Counters update in both inventory and main HUD.
- When a recipe is crafted:
  - Materials are deducted
  - Effect is applied (speed boost, passive Food generation, shield, etc.)

• 8. Deliverable

A functional Rezona game that includes ALL previous versions (V1, V2, V3) plus:

- Four active buttons (S, J, A, I) appearing only after astronaut exits ship
- Scan: cooldown 15s, reveals nearby resources
- Jump: cooldown 2s, brief Y-axis displacement
- Attack: cooldown 3s, horizontal plasma projectile
- Inventory modal with:
  - Material counters
  - Craftable recipes with costs and benefits
- Crafting system that deducts materials and applies permanent upgrades

